-- title:
--   Normality of the crossing model over a complete discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and assume $W$ is complete (in the sense of `IsAdicComplete`) for the adic filtration by its maximal ideal. Let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible and let $e$ be a natural number with $1 \le e$. Form the ring `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)`, namely the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\varpi^{e})$, where $C$ is the constant-coefficient inclusion of $W$; informally $W[\![u,v]\!]/(uv - \varpi^{e})$. The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions about this quotient: it is an integral domain, it is a local ring, and it is integrally closed in its field of fractions. Thus the crossing model at a uniformiser power over a complete discrete valuation base is a normal local domain; no regularity is claimed (for $e > 1$ the ring is an $A_{e-1}$ singularity).
--
--   This is the local structure statement for the standard crossing (node) model over a complete discrete valuation ring, the shape taken by the completed local ring of an arithmetic surface at an ordinary double point with thickness $e$. It supplies normality, locality and integrality of the base ring for the subsequent analysis of node annuli and of the singularities of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_isIntegrallyClosed_of_uniformizer_pow_of_isAdicComplete.lean

